[{"id":104618,"sender_id":252,"sender_full_name":"tomr","avatar_url":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/f5c490f629cf9a807f26939967aec109?d=identicon&version=1","content":"<p><a href=\"#narrow/channel/15-Mathematics.2C-Physics-.26-Philosophy/topic/What.20is.20denoted.20by.20operator.20bold-B.20in.20.22Differential.20cohomol.E2.80.A6/near/104618\">#1</a> I am trying to read https://ncatlab.org/schreiber/show/differential+cohomology+in+a+cohesive+topos (in my own path) and I see bold-B in many places (e.g. BH, where H is infinity-topos), but I have not managed to find name or explanation for it. There is place where B (though with indice) is called as de Rham complex, but I can not connect the dots.</p>\n<p>I am seeking just name for bold-B. No explanation is needed here - I will be able then found it myself as much as I need.</p>","timestamp":1673707316,"subject":"What is denoted by operator bold-B in \"Differential cohomol…","stream_id":15,"display_recipient":"Mathematics, Physics & Philosophy","reactions":[]},{"id":104619,"sender_id":1008,"sender_full_name":"Madeleine Birchfield","avatar_url":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/f759fe50e1d01fe5f7869048a1e486cc?d=identicon&version=1","content":"<p><a href=\"#narrow/channel/15-Mathematics.2C-Physics-.26-Philosophy/topic/What.20is.20denoted.20by.20operator.20bold-B.20in.20.22Differential.20cohomol.E2.80.A6/near/104619\">#2</a> I think the bold B stands for the <a href=\"https://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/delooping\">delooping</a> of an object. So for the infinity-topos H, BH would be the delooping of said infinity-topos.</p>","timestamp":1673714194,"subject":"What is denoted by operator bold-B in \"Differential cohomol…","stream_id":15,"display_recipient":"Mathematics, Physics & Philosophy","reactions":[]},{"id":104621,"sender_id":11,"sender_full_name":"Urs","avatar_url":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/b00d1ee17463af676c78974439b92471?d=identicon&version=1","content":"<p><a href=\"#narrow/channel/15-Mathematics.2C-Physics-.26-Philosophy/topic/What.20is.20denoted.20by.20operator.20bold-B.20in.20.22Differential.20cohomol.E2.80.A6/near/104621\">#3</a> The boldface <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"bold\">B</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\mathbf{B}</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6861em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathbf\">B</span></span></span></span> is for <em>delooping</em> of infinity-group objects in an infinity-topos <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"bold\">H</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\mathbf{H}</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6861em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathbf\">H</span></span></span></span>:</p>\n<p><span class=\"katex-display\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"block\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">G</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">u</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"bold\">H</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mi><munder><mo><mo><mover><mo><mo>≃</mo></mo><mo lspace=\"0em\" rspace=\"0em\"><mover><mo><mo>⟵</mo></mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Ω</mi></mover></mo></mover></mo></mo><mo lspace=\"0em\" rspace=\"0em\"><munder><mo><mo>⟶</mo></mo><mrow><mtext>  </mtext><mtext>  </mtext><mi mathvariant=\"bold\">B</mi><mtext>  </mtext><mtext>  </mtext></mrow></munder></mo></munder></mi><msubsup><mi mathvariant=\"bold\">H</mi><mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mo>∗</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">/</mi></mrow></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\n  \\mathrm{Groups}(\\mathbf{H})\n  \\underset{\\underset{\\;\\;\\mathbf{B}\\;\\;}{\\longrightarrow}}{\\overset{\\overset{\\Omega}{\\longleftarrow}}{\\simeq}}\n  \\mathbf{H}^{\\ast/}_{\\geq 1}\n</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:2.9703em;vertical-align:-1.2671em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathrm\">Groups</span></span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord mathbf\">H</span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mop op-limits\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:1.7032em;\"><span style=\"top:-3.1032em;margin-left:0em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3.7032em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mrel mtight\"><span class=\"mop op-limits mtight\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.511em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.0329em;margin-left:0em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size3 size1 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mspace mtight\" style=\"margin-right:0.4089em;\"></span><span class=\"mspace mtight\" style=\"margin-right:0.4089em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathbf mtight\">B</span><span class=\"mspace mtight\" style=\"margin-right:0.4089em;\"></span><span class=\"mspace mtight\" style=\"margin-right:0.4089em;\"></span></span></span></span><span style=\"top:-2.7em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span><span class=\"mop mtight\">⟶</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.8101em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span style=\"top:-3.7032em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3.7032em;\"></span><span><span class=\"mop\"><span class=\"mrel\"><span class=\"mop op-limits\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:1.7032em;\"><span style=\"top:-3em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span><span class=\"mop\">≃</span></span></span><span style=\"top:-3.6637em;margin-left:0em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mrel mtight\"><span class=\"mop op-limits mtight\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:1.3421em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.7em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span><span class=\"mop mtight\">⟵</span></span></span><span style=\"top:-3.411em;margin-left:0em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size3 size1 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">Ω</span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.011em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:1.2671em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathbf\">H</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:1.0448em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.4337em;margin-left:0em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mrel mtight\">≥</span><span class=\"mord mtight\">1</span></span></span></span><span style=\"top:-3.2198em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">∗</span><span class=\"mord mtight\">/</span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.3615em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></p>\n<p>according to <a href=\"https://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/May+recognition+theorem#RecognitionForGroupsInAnInfinityTopos\">this Prop.</a></p>","timestamp":1673718813,"subject":"What is denoted by operator bold-B in \"Differential cohomol…","stream_id":15,"display_recipient":"Mathematics, Physics & Philosophy","reactions":[]},{"id":104622,"sender_id":11,"sender_full_name":"Urs","avatar_url":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/b00d1ee17463af676c78974439b92471?d=identicon&version=1","content":"<p><a href=\"#narrow/channel/15-Mathematics.2C-Physics-.26-Philosophy/topic/What.20is.20denoted.20by.20operator.20bold-B.20in.20.22Differential.20cohomol.E2.80.A6/near/104622\">#4</a> I write it in boldface to indicate that this delooping is a “geometrically enriched” version of the classical classifying space construction which is traditionally denoted “<span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>B</mi><mi>G</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">B G</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0502em;\">B</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">G</span></span></span></span>”:</p>\n<p>If <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"bold\">H</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">h</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">G</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi></mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">∞</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\mathbf{H} = \\mathrm{SmoothGrpd}_\\infty</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6861em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathbf\">H</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.9386em;vertical-align:-0.2441em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathrm\">SmoothGrpd</span></span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.0573em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.4559em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">∞</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.2441em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span> and <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">G</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">G</span></span></span></span> a compact Lie group, then the underlying shape of <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"bold\">B</mi><mi>G</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\mathbf{B}G</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6861em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathbf\">B</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">G</span></span></span></span> (the <a href=\"https://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/delooping%20groupoid\">delooping groupoid</a> <a href=\"https://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/Lie%20groupoid\">Lie groupoid</a> of <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">G</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">G</span></span></span></span>) is the classifying space:</p>\n<p><span class=\"katex-display\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"block\"><semantics><mrow><mtext>ʃ</mtext><mi mathvariant=\"bold\">B</mi><mi>G</mi><mtext>  </mtext><mo>≃</mo><mtext>  </mtext><mi>B</mi><mi>G</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\n  ʃ\n  \\mathbf{B} G \n  \\;\\simeq\\;\n  B G\n</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6861em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">ʃ</span><span class=\"mord mathbf\">B</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">G</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">≃</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0502em;\">B</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">G</span></span></span></span></span></p>\n<p>This is Prop. 4.1.12 in <em><a href=\"https://ncatlab.org/schreiber/show/Equivariant%20principal%20infinity-bundles\">Equivariant principal infinity-bundles (schreiber)</a></em>. See also around  Prop. 0.2.1 there.</p>","timestamp":1673720886,"subject":"What is denoted by operator bold-B in \"Differential cohomol…","stream_id":15,"display_recipient":"Mathematics, Physics & Philosophy","reactions":[]}]